, "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Cleveland Clinic article describes what BMI is, how it\'s calculated, and its health uses and limitations; it does not mention \\"Spatial Scale\\" or any evidence about causal (or non-causal) relationships between an individual\'s ideal BMI and spatial scale. Because the source contains no information relevant to the proposed lack of causal linkage, it does not support the claim."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/news/publications/health-matters/is-bmi-accurate", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited URMC article discusses the accuracy, history, and health implications of BMI and questions the notion of an \\"ideal\\" BMI. It contains no information about \\"Spatial Scale\\" or about causal (or non-causal) relationships between BMI ideals and spatial scale. Therefore the source does not support the claim that there is no causal link between Individual Ideal BMI and Spatial Scale."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/bmi/adult-calculator/index.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited CDC BMI calculator page describes how BMI is calculated and its health categories; it does not mention \\"Individual Ideal BMI,\\" \\"Spatial Scale,\\" or any causal (or lack of) relationship between them. Because the source provides no evidence either linking or ruling out a causal connection, it does not support the claim of no relationship."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Individual Ideal BMI does not cause Spatial Scale to change, nor does Spatial Scale cause Individual Ideal BMI to change. There is no direct or indirect causal mechanism linking these two variables. Changes in one do not directly result in changes in the other.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.20570443758