c Rate (BMR) means the body becomes more efficient at conserving energy, so it actually reduces the Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE). Therefore, as BMR increases, TDEE decreases because the body learns to do more with less energy.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

