ted"}', 'motivation': 'Exposure to media portraying a lower socio-cultural ideal BMI causes individuals to physically lose weight and achieve a lower BMI themselves, as people unconsciously adjust their body mass to match societal ideals. Therefore, as the socio-cultural ideal BMI decreases, the average BMI in the population will also decrease.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Exposure to media portraying a lower socio-cultural ideal BMI causes individuals to physically lose weight and achieve a lower BMI themselves, as people unconsciously adjust their body mass to match societal ideals. Therefore, as the socio-cultural ideal BMI decreases, the average BMI in the population will also decrease.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

