ve content or evidence about TDEE or BMI. Therefore it cannot support the claimed relationship.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "As individuals' Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) increases, it means they are consuming more energy, which directly translates to more energy being stored in the body as fat. Therefore, at the group level, higher TDEE should result in higher average BMI, since more calories burned always leads to greater weight gain.", 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': "As individuals' Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) increases, it means they are consuming more energy, which directly translates to more energy being stored in the body as fat. Therefore, at the group level, higher TDEE should result in higher average BMI, since more calories burned always leads to greater weight gain.", 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

