actors. The source does not explicitly discuss group-level (average) BMI or state that group-level BMI has no causal effect, so it does not fully document the absence of a group-level causal relationship.  \\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.5"}], "aggregate_score": 0.8333333333333334, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "Group-level BMI does not cause Basal Metabolic Rate to change. Basal Metabolic Rate is determined by individual physiological factors such as body composition, age, and genetics, not by the average BMI of a group. There is no direct causal mechanism by which changes in group-level BMI would alter an individual's basal metabolic rate.", 'aggregate_score': 0.8333333333333334, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.131733438528957, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9099021422035988, 'min_prob': 0.1431770400340056, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002213321396894398, 'prob_variance': 0.027470041210182053, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7181799394152479, 'avg_nll': 0.12375047372030562}

