 and provides formulas based on an individual\'s weight/height/age/sex. It attributes BMR to individual physiological factors and does not identify group-average BMI as a determinant, so it supports the claim that group-level BMI does not cause changes in an individual\'s BMR."}], "aggregate_score": 0.8333333333333334, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "Group-level BMI does not cause Basal Metabolic Rate to change. Basal Metabolic Rate is determined by individual physiological factors such as body composition, age, and genetics, not by the average BMI of a group. There is no direct causal mechanism by which changes in group-level BMI would alter an individual's basal metabolic rate.", 'aggregate_score': 0.8333333333333334, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.131733438528957, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9099021422035988, 'min_prob': 0.1431770400340056, 'token_prob_slope': -0.002213321396894398, 'prob_variance': 0.027470041210182053, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.7181799394152479, 'avg_nll': 0.12375047372030562}

