   Properties: {'session_id': '1b5c2205-2f1e-4f9c-a83d-422f83f3d12e', 'prob_std': 0.17977518089552053, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6392078/', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK591031/', 'https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-27246-z', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10445668/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8778580716658074, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6392078/", "verdict": "SUPPORTED", "score": 1.0, "reason": "Judge 1: SUPPORTED - The cited study reports that differences in TDEE are driven by resting energy expenditure (REE) and physical activity energy expenditure (PAEE), notes that TDEE declines with weight loss because of reductions in REE and PAEE driven by lower body mass, and explicitly states the energy cost of activity is proportional to body weight. These findings are consistent with BMI affecting TDEE via mediators (REE and PAEE/physical activity) rather than implying an independent direct effect, supporting the motivation."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10445668/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited paper documents that TEE, BEE (BMR) and AEE are strongly dependent on body mass/BMI and explains mechanistic routes by which larger body mass alters energy expenditure (e.g., higher energy cost of movement raising AEE; scaling of basal metabolism with mass). That supports the claim that BMI influences TDEE via mediators such as basal metabolic rate and activity energy expenditure. However, the paper is observational/cross‑sectional and does not demonstrate the absence of any direct causal pathway from BMI to TDEE independent of those mediators. Thus the sources support the mediation argument but do not definitively establish that a direct causal link does not exist."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK591031/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited report describes TEE as the sum of REE (basal/resting metabolism), TEF, and physical activity, and documents that body size/composition (and thus BMI) affects REE and activity energy expenditure. It therefore supports the idea that BMI influences TEE primarily via those components (mediators). However, the source also reports a direct empirical association between increasing BMI/body mass and higher REE and higher absolute TEE in many studies, so it does not fully endorse the claim that there is no direct relationship at all."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-27246-z", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited paper shows total energy expenditure (TEE/TDEE) is strongly related to body composition (especially fat-free mass) and that, after adjusting for FFM/FM, TEE is repeatable and not predictive of short-term changes in body composition. It also frames TEE as the sum of basal metabolic processes and activity. These findings are consistent with the idea that body composition and components like basal metabolic rate and activity drive TEE, rather than BMI directly causing TEE changes. However, the study does not explicitly test a causal pathway from BMI to TDEE or formally demonstrate mediation via BMR and physical activity, nor does it directly use BMI as the exposure. Therefore the citation supports the motivation indirectly but does not provide direct causal evidence for the claimed mediation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.625, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Body Mass Index (BMI) does not directly cause Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) to change. The causal pathway operates through mediating variables such as Basal Metabolic Rate and Physical Activity Level, which are already included in the CLD. Therefore, there is no direct causal relationship from BMI to TDEE.', 'aggregate_score': 0.625, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.1313727128832451, 'mean_token_prob': 0.9135120828521136, 'min_prob': 0.15871255039665874, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00146372467416053, 'prob_variance': 0.03231911566601713, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0241424461473967, 'avg_nll': 0.12343168562586151}

